# What GitHub needs in order to render the profile — the allowlist. Everything not listed
# below is local-only, and nothing below can break the page, because the page only ever reads
# these: README.md · assets/svg/header.svg · divider.svg · footer.svg · assets/svg/panels/*.svg ·
# assets/svg/icons/cloud.svg, chip.svg, spark.svg · assets/svg/brands/amazonaws.svg.
# (The badges and glyphs under shields.io / cdn.simpleicons.org are fetched from those hosts.)
#
# So: retiring a card, or adding a glyph file, means editing that list too.

__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.DS_Store

# Working files — kept on disk, deliberately not in the remote:
#   .preview/            contact sheets rendered to check the cards by eye
#   DEVELOPING.md        how the generator works, for whoever picks this up next
#   TODO.md              the backlog of technologies not on the page yet
#   data/                the curated lists. The one thing he does not want public
#   scripts/             the generator. The page does not need it either — README.md and
#                        every card are committed, so the profile renders without it
#   assets/svg/brands/README.md
#                        the note on why amazonaws.svg is a local mark: prose, not a card.
#                        The mark it documents stays.
#
# Two paths are NOT render inputs but are deliberately kept: `.github/` (a workflow only runs
# when it is committed, so ignoring it would silently disable every check — gitleaks,
# actionlint, dependency review, Dependabot) and `LICENSE` (legal standing for a public repo).
#
# Everything here stays in the working tree, so `python3 scripts/build_readme.py` still runs
# locally; only the remote goes without. Note that **gitignore does not untrack a path that
# is already tracked** — it only stops a new one from being added — so each entry was also
# `git rm --cached`'d, which is how any of them comes back.
#
# The cost: nothing on the remote can rebuild the page, so "run `python3 scripts/build_readme.py`
# and commit" is a local habit and no CI check can catch a stale README. The generator is
# recoverable from git history at 18b0319.
.preview/
DEVELOPING.md
TODO.md
data/
scripts/
assets/svg/brands/README.md
